],"build":21,"channel":"beta","notes":["On Linux, right-click menus and toolbar menus such as the Pull and Push options now open.","On Linux, Northspline now uses the title area like on macOS: the toolbar replaces the separate title bar and the window buttons sit at the right end of the toolbar.","History no longer blanks to placeholder rows while a repository refreshes after a slow pull or fetch; the graph and the open commit stay visible and update when the new state is ready.","Switching repositories now shows the details of the selected commit right away.","Selecting a branch in the sidebar that the branch filter hides now shows it in History for as long as it stays selected.","Selecting a tag or the newest stash in the sidebar also shows it in a filtered History.","Repositories with a branch filter now show their last known History immediately when you switch to them or start the app.","The toolbar has a Branch button next to Pull and Push.","A new branch is checked out as soon as it is created, and your uncommitted changes come along. Clear \"Check out the new branch\" in the dialog to only create it.","Undo no longer offers to remove a branch you are currently on.","GitHub Enterprise Cloud accounts on a `ghe.com` address can now be connected.","When a hosting connection fails, Northspline now says why, for example that the server could not be reached or does not know the address, instead of \"unavailable\".","Repository tabs that are not selected are now separated by a thin line, so each one reads as a tab.","A configured diff renderer that does not read its input no longer falls back to the built-in diff at random."],"tag":"v0.1.0-beta.20-21","version":"0.1.0-beta.20"},{"assets":[{"architecture":"x86_64","bytes":15530488,"file":"Northspline-0.1.0-beta.19-20-linux-x86_64.AppImage","format":"AppImage","minimum_system":"glibc 2.35 and Git 2.39","platform":"linux","sha256":"d650c7fb588196cfc34e5086a7c78025c6345affdb76db55d018e9459fc3df6a","url":"https://github.c